Weaknesses

The numbers you saw are from fake data. Never quote the 0.917 coverage or the MAE figures. Real metrics appear only after python -m pipeline.build, and they may be worse.
Terra-only years (before mid-2002). MODIS counts there are structurally lower, and the app widens the intervals for them. This still needs a proper treatment.
Small areas. When an area has too few hotspots to calibrate, the app borrows the regional model and doubles the interval, and says so.
Speed. An analysis takes about 0.7 s on demo data. Real data will be larger, so a pre-aggregated grid table is the next optimisation.
The independent check isn’t built yet. The Landsat or Sentinel-2 burn-scar validation is a separate job, and Earth Engine access takes time. Someone on your team should start on it now.
The 3D Montréal page. It doesn’t satisfy this brief, which asks for any selectable area. Treat it as optional polish.
