Why it happens: All ~240 countries across 2000–2026 (MODIS + VIIRS S-NPP + NOAA-20) total 150–250+ million detections. In pipeline/ingest.py, holding every country-year DataFrame in memory in parts = [] and calling pd.concat(parts) + drop_duplicates() at the end spikes RAM usage past 16–32 GB, causing the OS to kill the Python process silently (exit code 137 on Mac/Linux or a silent exit on Windows) right after the downloads finish.

Your downloaded CSVs are safe: Everything already downloaded in data/raw/ is cached on disk and will not need to be re-downloaded.

2. Wrong Python Interpreter (python -q app.py)
VS Code's top-right Run ▶ button runs python -q app.py using whichever interpreter is selected in the bottom-right status bar of VS Code. If .venv wasn't selected there (or if it exited with ModuleNotFoundError), it ran outside your virtual environment.

